# CITATION.cff -- how to cite sremu (WP12). Citation File Format 1.2.0.
#
# Released under the MIT licence (2026-10-15). Add the Zenodo DOI and a preferred-citation
# pointing to the arXiv preprint once they exist.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use sremu, please cite it using the metadata below. sremu is pre-release software
  released under the MIT licence.
type: software
title: "sremu: Smart Radio Environment EMUlator"
version: 0.1.0.dev0
abstract: >-
  sremu is a software-only, IQ-level radio-environment emulator for reconfigurable
  intelligent surfaces (RIS). RIS configurations are timestamped runtime commands from an
  external controller, applied at an exact, logged sample on every receiver; per-state RIS
  responses can be imported from measurements; wall-clock behaviour is measured and
  reported.
authors:
  - given-names: Galaba
    family-names: Vamsi
    email: galabav@iitbhilai.ac.in
    affiliation: Indian Institute of Technology Bhilai, India
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Galabavamsi/sremu"
keywords:
  - reconfigurable intelligent surface
  - smart radio environment
  - RIS
  - IQ-level emulation
  - software-defined radio
  - channel emulation
  - controller in the loop
